    {
      "id": "section-6a3869264938951d7e3233d4",
      "kind": "content",
      "columns": [
        {
          "start": 1,
          "span": 12,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "html": "<h2>The Project</h2><p>Lendit is a peer-to-peer marketplace built to help people rent and lend everyday items within their local community. The idea was simple: turn the things you rarely use into opportunities for others, and for yourself. From cameras and speakers to power tools and bicycles, Lendit connects neighbors through trust and convenience.</p><p>I was responsible for the full product design process, shaping both the user experience and the visual identity. My work covered UX research, user flows, wireframes, and high-fidelity UI design for web and mobile. I also developed the design system, defined component logic for developers, and established a visual language that communicates warmth, reliability, and belonging.</p><p><strong>Timeline:</strong> Aug–Oct 2025 (Phase 1 — research to high-fidelity) · Oct 2025–present (testing &amp; iteration, support)</p><p><strong>Role:</strong> UI/UX Designer</p>"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "section-6a3879d94938951d7e381c32",
      "kind": "content",
      "columns": [
        {
          "start": 1,
          "span": 5,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "html": "<h2>The Context</h2><p>Lendit was founded to solve a common problem: people have useful items sitting idle, while others nearby need them for a short time. The platform needed to feel trustworthy, easy to use, and rewarding for both sides.</p>"
            }
          ]
        },
