      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "section-6a392f524938951d7e79b921",
      "kind": "content",
      "columns": [
        {
          "start": 1,
          "span": 12,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "html": "<h2>Undestanding the audience</h2><p>I began this project by understanding how people currently access tools and items in their daily lives.</p><p>Unlike traditional marketplaces, borrowing is often informal — people ask friends, delay projects, or end up buying items they only use once.</p><p>This revealed a key behavior: people don’t actively look for “borrowing platforms” — they just want a quick and reliable way to get what they need.</p>"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "section-6a3938c14938951d7e7e2746",
      "kind": "content",
      "columns": [
        {
          "start": 3,
          "span": 8,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "html": "<h2>Most people don’t need to own things — they just need access to them at the right time.</h2>"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "section-6a393a144938951d7e7e7cba",
      "kind": "content",
      "columns": [
        {
          "start": 1,
          "span": 6,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "html": "<h2>Competitive Analysis</h2><p>I reviewed the platforms Lendit actually competes with — Hygglo (formerly Fat Llama), the local food-sharing app Olio, and informal Facebook lending groups — and pulled UX-pattern references from mature marketplaces like Airbnb and Vinted to set a clear interaction and aesthetic direction.</p><p>Mapping each player on two axes — how deep their trust model runs, and how local they are — surfaced the gap: nobody pairs a full trust stack with a genuinely hyperlocal model. That open territory is where Lendit sits. A capability benchmark against Hygglo and Olio sharpened it further, comparing the trust and transaction features that decide whether strangers will transact — and confirming where Lendit could lead.</p>"
            }
          ]
        },
