    {
      "id": "section-6a39b6a14938951d7ec1df30",
      "kind": "content",
      "columns": [
        {
          "start": 1,
          "span": 12,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "html": "<h2>Secondary research</h2><p>Before I drew a single screen, I grounded the work in what already exists and how people actually behave.</p><p>I reviewed peer to peer marketplaces and everyday borrowing habits to understand what makes these exchanges feel easy and safe.</p><p>I studied how platforms like Vinted and Airbnb reduce friction and build trust between strangers, from clear expectations to lightweight safeguards.</p><p>In parallel, I looked at real life behavior, how people borrow today by asking friends, delaying tasks, or buying items they will barely use again.</p>"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "section-6a3c48f6cb0dae1732c01552",
      "kind": "content",
      "columns": [
        {
          "start": 1,
          "span": 12,
