        {
          "start": 8,
          "span": 5,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "html": "<h2>User Personas</h2><p>Lendit is a two-sided marketplace, so I designed for two-sided demand. Three lender archetypes (supply) and three borrower archetypes (demand) kept every decision anchored to a real motivation — earning safely on one side, accessing affordably on the other.</p>"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "section-6a41ae0cfa8b4c01d55025b6",
      "kind": "content",
      "columns": [
        {
          "start": 1,
          "span": 5,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "html": "<h2>User Flow</h2><p>The trust lifecycle is two sided, one entry, two roles. I designed both the lender and borrower journeys to converge on a single review moment, because that review powers every trust signal across the product.</p>"
            }
          ]
        },
