        {
          "start": 1,
          "span": 12,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "html": "<h2>Systemise</h2>"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "section-6a42f2398163f948cff42585",
      "kind": "content",
      "columns": [
        {
          "start": 1,
          "span": 4,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "html": "<h2>Visual Consistency</h2>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "start": 5,
          "span": 8,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "html": "<p>Lendit was designed as one system, not a pile of screens. Instead of rebuilding the same patterns, I focused on reusable components built from shared primitives. When the UI was nearly identical, I treated it as one component with clear variants, not dozens of near duplicates. Style is defined through tokens, colour, type, spacing, radius, and elevation, set once and inherited everywhere, keeping 100 plus components and 500 plus variables coherent.</p><p>Iconography followed the same approach. I standardized on stroke based icons from Tabler Icons and Lucide, using a shared 24px and 1.5px spec. This created a consistent visual language across the product, with stroke weight, cap style, and colour kept aligned instead of overridden icon by icon.</p>"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
